<section class="container section" id="work" aria-labelledby="work-title">
<div class="section-head"><div><span class="section-no">Selected practice</span><h2 id="work-title">A few things taking shape.</h2></div><p>Concept studies exploring clear interfaces, useful interactions and a strong visual point of view. These are illustrative projects, not client case studies.</p></div>
<div class="project-list">
<article class="project"><div class="project-copy"><p class="project-type">01 / Brand and web concept</p><h3>Good Ground</h3><p class="project-description">A considered identity and shop direction for a fictional small-batch home and garden label. Natural tones, a calm rhythm and clear product storytelling.</p><ul class="tags" aria-label="Skills used"><li>Visual direction</li><li>HTML and CSS</li><li>Responsive design</li></ul></div>
<div class="project-visual visual-brand" role="img" aria-label="Concept layout for Good Ground, a fictional home and garden label"><div><p class="mock-label">Objects for everyday living</p><p class="mock-title">Good<br>ground.</p><div class="mock-bottom"><span class="mock-label">Made to be lived with</span><span class="mock-circle" aria-hidden="true"></span></div></div></div></article>
<article class="project"><div class="project-copy"><p class="project-type">02 / Interface concept</p><h3>Clearwork</h3><p class="project-description">A fictional project-planning interface that puts the next useful action first. A simple information hierarchy, quiet status treatment and readable working space.</p><ul class="tags" aria-label="Skills used"><li>Interface design</li><li>Interaction states</li><li>Accessibility</li></ul></div>
<div class="project-visual visual-dashboard" role="img" aria-label="Concept planning dashboard with abstract project panels"><div><div class="dash-top"><span class="dash-title">Clearwork</span><span class="mock-label">Today / Overview</span></div><p class="dash-headline">Make room<br>for good work.</p><div class="dash-sheet" aria-hidden="true"><div class="dash-block">Projects<div class="dash-line"></div><div class="dash-line short"></div></div><div class="dash-block">In progress<div class="dash-line"></div><div class="dash-line short"></div></div><div class="dash-block">Up next<div class="dash-line"></div><div class="dash-line short"></div></div></div></div></div></article>
<article class="project"><div class="project-copy"><p class="project-type">03 / Editorial web concept</p><h3>Open Field Notes</h3><p class="project-description">A fictional digital journal for observing places and everyday life. Strong typographic hierarchy, an unhurried reading pace and a flexible article layout.</p><ul class="tags" aria-label="Skills used"><li>Editorial layout</li><li>Typography</li><li>Semantic HTML</li></ul></div>
<div class="project-visual visual-publication" role="img" aria-label="Concept spread for Open Field Notes with a botanical motif and editorial headline"><div class="pub-sheet"><div class="pub-image" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 200 240" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M95 228C93 175 104 103 110 20" stroke="#354d3c" stroke-width="3"/><path d="M105 118C57 122 37 95 36 57C77 62 102 81 105 118Z" fill="#849b78"/><path d="M101 163C144 159 168 131 170 94C132 101 108 126 101 163Z" fill="#657d5a"/><path d="M109 75C133 79 150 64 153 38C131 43 115 55 109 75Z" fill="#a4ad84"/><path d="M95 196C66 190 51 168 51 145C77 151 92 169 95 196Z" fill="#748d67"/></svg></div><div><p class="mock-label">The slow observation</p><p class="pub-heading">Pay attention to what grows.</p><p class="pub-copy">Short notes on seasons, surfaces and the things we almost miss.</p></div></div></div></article>
</div></section>
<section class="container section" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-title"><div class="about-layout"><div><span class="section-no">A little about me</span><h2 id="about-title">Curiosity, then craft.</h2></div><div class="about-copy"><p class="about-statement">I like the point where a useful idea becomes something clear, tactile and easy to use.</p><p>I’m building my practice in web development and design. I care about readable type, thoughtful spacing, semantic structure and the details that help a website feel welcoming rather than overwhelming.</p><p>This portfolio is a work in progress. The projects above are concept studies, and this section is a starting point for a more personal story.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="container section" id="skills" aria-labelledby="skills-title"><div class="skills-layout"><div><span class="section-no">How I work</span><h2 id="skills-title">Tools and approach.</h2></div><div class="skill-groups">
<div class="skill-row"><h3>Structure</h3><p>Semantic HTML, accessible content, useful document hierarchy.</p></div>
<div class="skill-row"><h3>Presentation</h3><p>CSS, responsive layouts, typography, colour and spacing systems.</p></div>
<div class="skill-row"><h3>Interaction</h3><p>JavaScript fundamentals, navigation and clear interface states.</p></div>
<div class="skill-row"><h3>Practice</h3><p>Iterative learning, careful testing and attention to small details.</p></div>
</div></div></section>
